Syntax: defchar [<path>]Function:defines a new Charset for VT220 TerminalsOptions: none"chardef" does not designate and map the defined charset.Syntax of chardefinition:"clear"	clear the old charset "charset"[0-~]	define a name for the new charset (default '<')<Number>:					number of the character['*'|'.']*					'*' means pixel on "end"						send the charset to the terminalExample:Define charset 'X' witch character 33, 34 and 90.charsetX33:.......*......**.....***..*******************..****.....*.............34:*.*.*.*..*.*.*.**.*.*.*..*.*.*.*90:**..**..**..**....**..**..**..****..**..**..**....**..**..**..****..**..**..**..end